# =============================================================================
# Code owners for p-SWAMP
# =============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
#
#   A list of file patterns, each with one or more owners: the people who know
#   a given corner of the repo well enough that they would want to know when it
#   changes.
#
# HOW IT INTERACTS WITH PULL REQUESTS
#
#   GitHub reads this file whenever a pull request is opened against main. If
#   the branch touches files somebody owns, that person is added as a reviewer
#   AUTOMATICALLY and gets a notification. If you want to keep tabs on a certain part of this repo
#   add yourself as owner on that directory so that you get notified about new PRs that touch that code.
#
#   main is protected, but code-owner approval is
#   NOT required to merge pull requests. The point of our PRs is
#   to get the right eyes on a change, not to add a waiting step.
#
# ADDING YOURSELF
#
#   If you own an area, or keep being surprised by changes to some directory,
#   add a line for it. A few things to know:
#
#     - The LAST matching pattern wins, so broad rules go first and specific
#       ones further down. Only that one pattern applies — matches are not
#       combined.
#     - Paths starting with / are anchored to the repo root; a trailing /
#       matches everything under a directory.
#     - An owner must be a GitHub user or team with write access to this repo.
#       GitHub silently ignores a line naming anyone else.
#     - This file only takes effect once it is on main. Edits to it on a
#       feature branch do not apply to that branch's own PR.
#
#   Syntax reference: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# =============================================================================
