# The generated api contract between the web client and the server. Both files are
# machine-written and committed, and a diff here is the visible form of "the shape
# other teams code against just changed" -- which is exactly the change worth a
# second pair of eyes. Add yourself if you consume this api.
/doc/api/                            @thomanil
/app/server-python/src/api_contract.py  @thomanil

# Deploy manifest for the local minikube cluster.
/k8s/          @thomanil

# CI pipeline and agent/copilot instructions.
/.github/      @thomanil

# Dependency manifests and lockfiles, both halves of the repo. These patterns
# are unanchored, so they match at every depth: the web client's package.json /
# package-lock.json, and every Python pyproject.toml / uv.lock (the workspace
# root and its members, and the desktop package under desktop/).
# A dependency bump is the change most worth a second pair of eyes — it is
# usually produced wholesale by uv run pswamp deps update, so the diff is
# large, machine-written, and the only place a supply-chain surprise can enter.
package.json        @thomanil
package-lock.json   @thomanil
pyproject.toml      @thomanil
uv.lock             @thomanil

# The reference subapp -- the scaffold example both AGENTS.md and
# doc/the-client-server-api.md point at, and the end-to-end smoke test of the
# client-server stack. It is meant to stay boring and current, so a change to
# either half is worth a look.
/app/client-web/src/pages/reference-subapp/  @thomanil
/app/server-python/src/reference_subapp/     @thomanil
